      "what_a_flip_is": "A flip is a disagreement between one arm's prediction on the clean test tree and the same arm's prediction on the expanded test tree, for the same example_id. The two texts make the same claim under rules whose declared invariant is that they change neither tense, person, certainty nor polarity, so a flip is an error on one side of the pair, whichever side that is. No label is read to see one.",
